{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1456887-v20-replicating-path-powers-with-rituals","id":1456887,"title":"[V20] Replicating Path powers with rituals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-08-15T11:30:47-07:00","id":1456887,"title":"[V20] Replicating Path powers with rituals","content":"Let's say I have Movement of the Mind for my primary path, but want to use Technomancy's Remote Access for one specific job. Or I want some basic zombies <i>and</i> the ability to summon wraiths but I only want one power from both the Sepulchre and Bone paths and would rather put my xp into another path. Maybe I'm not even Giovanni so I don't really have access to these paths (unless all the necromancers actually have access to all the paths, and they just call them different names, I guess. I mean Anarch sorcery and Assamite sorcery apparently use Thaumaturgy paths, so eh.)<br /> <br /> The obvious answer is do an insane amount of playing and hope your character doesn't get offed while you gather a few hundred xp and get multiple paths, even if you're only doing them for one power out of five.<br /> <br /> But there is some basis in the text for paths having the streamlined version of a ritual. In necromancy at least. Reveal the Catene from the Cenotaph Path is the quick'n'easy version of Ritual of the Unearthed Fetter. Similarly Shroudsight and Lifeless Tongues lets you spy on wraiths without a mirror or a candle and a pair of scissors. The path is also much more useful for that purpose.<br /> <br /> What should the caveats should be?<br /> Should the rituals be the same level as the power, or higher? (Reveal the Catene is **, its equivalent ritual is level 3)<br /> Also, should the ritual be weaker in effect than the path?<br /> Are there any paths or abilities that shouldn't be replicable?<br /> <br /> I'm currently thinking that I'd be putting such rituals at one level higher (meaning that the fifth and most powerful dot in a path requires mastery of that path with no work arounds, which is fair, tbh). All of them require time spent concentrating, taking anything from a few minutes (level 2) sometimes to a week or even a month (level 5) to complete. There's also a lot more resources to hunt down and organise on top of any rolls, willpower and blood required. I don't know about making it weaker, I think the requirements are restrictive enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 08-15-2021, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-15T12:43:21-07:00","id":1456900,"title":"","content":"If it exists, there's a ritual for it. <br /> <br /> <br /> I wouldn't make such rituals a level higher. More, the price comes down to taking a longer time to cast, potentially with other complications like different materials needed. &quot;remote access&quot; should at the least require you to have a piece of the object you want to mess with, or at least a device that is connected to the subject (an IP address or wifi router may do)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-15T18:53:18-07:00","id":1456921,"title":"","content":"IIRC paths are 'quick and dirty' whereas rituals allow for more stuff to be done at a greater level of power, at the cost of more time and complexity (although blood cost may or may not be there depending on what is achieved.) Rituals allow you to do more, but paths allow you to do it faster. If Rituals are hex editing, then paths would be something like Cheat engine. <br /> <br /> That means that for every path there probably is one or more rituals to do the same thing, only better. As long as you're willing not to hurry things or aren't in an emergency and have minutes, hours or longer to spare. <br /> <br /> This also means rituals are more predmeditated and planned and are probably the culmination of a sequence of events, rather than something you spend a blood point and invoke more often than not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}